 ## Get set up
 
-1. Install with `/add-plugin pstack` in chat, or from Customize in the sidebar.
-2. Run [`/setup-pstack`](../setup-pstack/SKILL.md). It asks for a reasoning budget, maps a model to each role, and writes a rule. The rule applies to new chats. Then it offers once each to generate a verification skill and a formal verification skill for the project, unless the project already has one.
+1. Install the pstack bundle with Skillbox in the project, then run `skillbox sync` to generate `.agents/skills/`. The bundle README owns the exact commands; this help page only routes questions.
+2. Run [`/setup-pstack`](../setup-pstack/SKILL.md). It asks for a reasoning budget, maps a seat to each role from `bl agent catalog`, and writes `.botlake/pstack-roles.md`. The table applies to new agent runs. Then it offers once each to generate a verification skill and a formal verification skill for the project, unless the project already has one.
 3. Start a real task with `/poteto-mode`, a goal, and a check that can pass or fail.
 
